%----  fewbody: suite of cold-collapse 3-10 body problems.
%
% Deliberately identical to plummer_binaries.params except for the four values below the
% initial condition forces: the two tests are meant to differ only in their IC, so that a
% disagreement between them is attributable to the dynamics and not to a run setting.
%
% ErrTolIntAccuracy is 0.01, the value a production STARFORGE run actually integrates at:
% begrun.cc defaults it to 0.02, and GRAVITY_ACCURATE_FEWBODY_INTEGRATION (which
% SINGLE_STAR_STARFORGE_DEFAULTS turns on) then clamps it to 0.01. So this measures what the
% science runs deliver, not a tuned-down best case. The acceleration timestep goes as
% sqrt(ErrTolIntAccuracy) (timestep.cc: dt = sqrt(2 eta h / |a|)), so each 4x cut in the
% tolerance halves the step. Read from this file only because DEVELOPER_MODE is set in
% Config.sh; without it GIZMO ignores the line and applies the same 0.02-clamped-to-0.01.
% Earlier scan points are kept under archive/ (5e-3, 1.25e-3).
%
% PartAllocFactor is enormous (200) on purpose: these problems have 3-10 particles, so the
% allocation is a few hundred slots either way, and the default 2.5 truncates to a size for
% which GIZMO can find no legal domain decomposition on 2 ranks ('No domain decomposition that
% stays within memory bounds is possible').
%
% TimeMax = 0.1 is ~19 free-fall times of the median system (t_ff ranges 2.3e-3 to 1.2e-2
% across the suite), long enough for every system to collapse, form a hard binary and eject
% members. MaxSizeTimestep is scaled from plummer_binaries by the same TimeMax ratio.
% Plummer cluster of equal-mass circular binaries (Type 5 stars).
% Units: pc - km/s - Msun, so G = 4.302e-3 in code units.
% N=256 binaries, M_star=1 Msun, M_cluster=512 Msun, a_cluster=1 pc.
% Half-mass crossing time t_cross ~ 3.24 code time units (~ 3.17 Myr).
% TimeMax = 32.4 covers ~10 cluster crossings; binary period (1000 AU, 2 Msun)
% is ~0.023 code units, so ~1400 binary orbits over the run.
% TimeBetSnapshot = t_cross / 10 -> 100 snapshots over the test.
% Plummer-equivalent softening = 6.43 AU = 3.117e-5 pc (= 18 AU / 2.8), so the
% actual cubic-spline kernel radius is the desired 18 AU.
%
InitCondFile                       fewbody_ics
OutputDir                          output
TimeMax                            0.1
BoxSize                            300
TimeBetSnapshot                    0.002
TimeOfFirstSnapshot                0
TimeBegin                          0
TimeBetStatistics                  0.002
MaxSizeTimestep                    1e-4
MinSizeTimestep                    1e-12
ErrTolIntAccuracy                  0.01
ErrTolTheta                        0.5
ErrTolForceAcc                     0.0025
CourantFac                         0.4
MaxRMSDisplacementFac              0.125
TreeDomainUpdateFrequency          0.1
DesNumNgb                          32
MaxNumNgbDeviation                 1
MaxMemSize                         2000
PartAllocFactor                    200
BufferSize                         100
ResubmitOn                         0
ResubmitCommand                    none
UnitLength_in_cm                   3.085678e+18
UnitMass_in_g                      1.989e+33
UnitVelocity_in_cm_per_s           100000
Softening_Type0                    3.117e-5
Softening_Type1                    3.117e-5
Softening_Type2                    3.117e-5
Softening_Type3                    3.117e-5
Softening_Type4                    3.117e-5
Softening_Type5                    3.117e-5
Softening_Type0_MaxPhysLimit       3.117e-5
Softening_Type1_MaxPhysLimit       3.117e-5
Softening_Type2_MaxPhysLimit       3.117e-5
Softening_Type3_MaxPhysLimit       3.117e-5
Softening_Type4_MaxPhysLimit       3.117e-5
Softening_Type5_MaxPhysLimit       3.117e-5
AGS_DesNumNgb                      32
AGS_MaxNumNgbDeviation             1
CritPhysDensity                    1e13
CpuTimeBetRestartFile              30
% Cap sink accretion-search at the softening kernel radius (18 AU = 8.726e-5 pc).
% With no gas in this test the default 5 pc search radius wastes huge amounts of
% tree-walking; shrinking it to the softening scale eliminates that overhead.
SinkMaxAccretionRadius             8.726e-5
